# ===========================================================================
#  What is deliberately NOT in this repository, and why
# ===========================================================================
#
# 1. THE CORPUS.  txt/ and data/corpus.txt are Liu Cixin's complete works in
#    plain text. They are copyrighted. Redistributing them here would be
#    wrong, and a repository that ships them gets taken down. Supply your own
#    legally obtained copies and rebuild with scripts/build_corpus.py and
#    scripts/prepare_data.py (see README).
#
# 2. THINGS THAT ARE LARGE.  downloads/ is a 2.5 GB offline torch wheel,
#    ref/ is a third-party reference clone, and llama2.c/out_*/ holds training
#    checkpoints. GitHub hard-rejects any single file over 100 MB, and none of
#    this is needed to build the firmware.
#
# 3. THINGS THE BUILD REGENERATES.  .pio/, __pycache__/.
#
# 4. DEBUG RESIDUE.  The root *.log files are captured serial output from
#    hardware bring-up. Interesting once, noise forever.
#
# Everything excluded here is rebuildable; the README says how.
# ===========================================================================

# --- PlatformIO / Python build output ---------------------------------------
.pio/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- editor state -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch

# --- corpus: copyrighted, must not be redistributed -------------------------
txt/
data/corpus.txt
data/tok8192/

# --- large / third-party ----------------------------------------------------
downloads/
ref/

# --- training output: 10-100 MB checkpoints and fp32 blobs ------------------
llama2.c/out_liucixin/
llama2.c/out_liucixin_v2/

# --- intermediate quantization blobs ---------------------------------------
# llama2.c/model_esp_v2.bin IS committed on purpose: it is the deployed
# artwork's weights (3.6 MB), so the repo can be flashed without retraining.
llama2.c/q8_*.bin
llama2.c/model.bin
llama2.c/model_esp_smoke.bin

# --- junction into ../data; recreate it with: -------------------------------
#     cmd /c mklink /J llama2.c\data data
llama2.c/data

# --- serial capture residue -------------------------------------------------
*.log
dl_report.json
